  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1814.08 Duration and Renewal of Training Provider and Training Course Approvals",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1814.08 Duration and Renewal of Training Provider and Training Course Approvals.\n\n(a) Training provider and training course approval shall be effective for one year from the date of issuance as indicated on the written approval.\n\n(b) If the training provider wishes to renew the approval, the training provider shall:\n\n(1) Submit a completed application for renewal, on the “Application for Asbestos Training Provider and Courses” form specified in Env-A 1814.02(a), no later than 30 days prior to the expiration date of the current approval, including the information specified in Env-A 1814.02 and Env-A 1814.04;\n\n(2) Attach any additional information and documentation required by this chapter, including a list of the type of asbestos training courses offered in the past year with the number of students that successfully completed the courses; and\n\n(3) Apply for renewal no later than 3 years after the expiration date of the previous approval.\n\n(c) The department shall not accept a renewal application from a previously approved training provider whose approval expired more than 3 years prior to the date of the renewal application, but shall inform the person that if approval is desired, a new application shall be submitted pursuant to Env-A 1814.02 and Env-A 1804.04.\n\n(d) The department shall process a renewal application as specified in Env-A 1814.07.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
